<title>DENMARK: Danish central bank '96 profit up to 5.9 bln crown.</title>
<headline>Danish central bank '96 profit up to 5.9 bln crown.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Denmark's central bank, the National Bank, said on Thursday that it ended 1996 with a surplus of 5.867 billion crowns, compared to a surplus of 4.805 billion crowns the year before.</p>
<p>In its 1996 annual report the bank said it put 1.09 billion crowns into its new currency regulation fund, 1.43 billion crowns into its contingency fund and the rest, 3.34 billlion, was transferred to state coffers.</p>
<p>It said net foreign exchange reserves rose by 21 billion crowns in 1996 to 85 billion crowns.</p>
<p>--Steve Weizman, Copenhagen newsroom +45 33969650</p>
</text>
